for years star wars fans have dreamed of  seeing some of the sagas many cancelled  projects from the underworld tv series  to george lucas's sequel trilogy would  they be just as excited for a droid  spin-off for an ewok video game though  we'll let you decide  james mangold's boba fett movie could be  the greatest last the star wars fandom  will ever suffer the celebrated director  and academy award nominated writer was  the man who delivered the suburb final  chapter in wolverine's cinematic story  with logan and there can be no doubt  that he would have brought a fantastic  boba fett story to the screen mangold  proved with both logan and 310 to uma  that he can make modern westerns with  equal parts brutal action and thematic  heft while the mandalorian has certainly  offered fans a more western inspired  taste of the star wars universe a  feature would have allowed mangold to  flesh out a more epic story this movie  might even have been the film that  brought the franchise back into the best  screenplay category at the oscars given  mangold's previous historic nomination  for logan of course there's no way to  know for sure but that doesn't make this  particular last any less painful  a wookie focused movie was an idea that  george lucas came up with when initially  developing star wars somewhat  disastrously this idea eventually led to  the star wars holiday special  but with the right script and a creative  director this could be something far  superior to that particular outing  lucas's original idea was a film that  didn't focus on chewbacca but instead  allowed for a more ethnographic study of  wookies no one knows exactly what the  story would have been but the wookie  homeworld of kashyyyk has a significant  history of occupations and uprisings  that would lend itself perfectly to a  wookiee focus story the movie would  likely dive into their culture while  also offering the classic rebels versus  oppressor storyline that's such a staple  of the star wars saga and based on the  battle on kashyyyk in revenge of the  sith it probably would have looked great  too of course you've got to consider the  fact that wookie's only speaking  unintelligible grouse while this may  seem like a problem it's also an  opportunity for something really  exciting and somewhat avant-garde a lack  of spoken dialogue has driven some  fascinating movies such as 2014's the  tribe in which the characters only speak  in ukrainian sign language doing  something similar with the wookies could  have been a huge success or a terrible  failure but it would have been  fascinating either way  a droid only movie was another concept  for a one-off film that lucas had in the  70s one that also could have developed  into something truly special for the  franchise the obvious reference point  for this kind of thing is wally which  proves that you can tell a story that  focused on robots and still be engaging  and emotionally impactful the major  differences of course are that lucas  envisioned a movie with no human  characters at all as well as the fact  that many droids can speak in languages  that viewers can understand while the  film would not have made room for any  human characters it would have allowed  for comprehensible dialogue between the  droids like the wookie focused movie the  idea here was not to extend the stories  of droids that viewers knew already but  to tell an entirely separate story that  explored how droids interact with one  another when other life forms aren't  around considering audiences have only  been given glimpse of this kind of thing  in existing films it's likely that many  fans would have clamored at the chance  to see a little more  star wars underworld was a live-action  tv series that was going to take fans  into the murky depths of the star wars  universe the show promised to be a more  adult take on the saga offering up fresh  and exciting stories that weren't solely  focused on the skywalker clan it would  have taken place between the end of  revenge of the sith and the beginning of  a new hope and explored the dark  underbelly of coruscant you want to buy  some death sticks you don't want to sell  me death sticks i don't want to sell you  death sticks you want to go home and  rethink your life i want to go home and  rethink my life the idea this time  however was to offer something much more  morally ambiguous and narratively  complex than the films themselves a  small screen format and long-form  structure of television storytelling  would have allowed for more dialogue and  character-driven stories the creator's  ambitions for the show were impressive  too with frequent lucas collaborator  rick mccallum telling sfx magazine the  shows we aspire to are the sopranos the  wire battlestar galactica deadwood all  of that group while disney has now moved  star wars into the world of prestige tv  with the mandalorian that show still  feels pretty pg when compared with the  shows mccallum mentioned for now we can  hope that the fact that the mandalorians  runaway success might be a source of  hope for underworld's future  george lucas says sequal trilogy would  have been very different from the one  disney ended up producing as revealed by  lucas in interviews for the book the  star wars archives arguably the most  exciting aspect of his trilogy ideas  were the villains lucas's big bads would  have been darth maul and his new  apprentice the tweedlek darth talon in  these movies maul's power would not have  been governmental but instead criminal  lucas envisioned a power vacuum after  the fall of the empire that would have  been filled by more he would have united  the criminal world and became the  godfather of crime in the universe the  films also would have placed leia at the  heart of the story working to combat  maul's influence on the galaxy and  rebuild the republic meanwhile luke  would have been attempting to rebuild  the jedi order from the remaining jedi  who survived order 66 finding him on a  mission to locate potential jedi  throughout the galaxy saga would then  reveal that it's actually leia who was  the chosen one as she is the one who  brings harmony to the galaxy through the  creation of a true republic it's almost  certain we'll never get to see these  stories play out now that we already  have a sequel trilogy but with dc and  the mcu both opening multiverses what's  to stop star wars from joining the fun  thanks to the announcement that  lucasfilm games are remaking the 2003  classic rpg knights of the old republic  there have been rumors abound regarding  the long-lasting knights of the old  republic 3. sadly nothing is yet  concrete and there's no way to know what  the game might look like given that it's  been more than 15 years since the last  installment but according to chris  avalon lead designer and writer on  knights of the old republic 2 there was  always an idea for a third game  according to him the story would have  focused on an ancient and even more evil  group of sith of course this won't come  as a surprise to fans of the old  republic games considering the second  installment teases a hidden cabal of  true sith on more than one occasion  certainly one of the most exciting  aspects of the third game will be  unraveling the mysteries of these hugely  powerful beings each of whom has to be  given a unique origin story sadly no one  can even be sure whether these ideas  will be a part of knights of the old  republic 3 even if it does one day  appear but that won't stop fans from  dreaming  star wars 1313 seems like it would have  been the video game equivalent of  underworld with the game even apparently  aiming for an m rating players would  have controlled boba fett as he  traversed the 13th 13th level of  coruscant and unravelled a massive  conspiracy like underworld the game  would have been more adult-oriented by  virtue of its brutal violence as well as  a more complex character-oriented story  like the cancelled boba fett movie the  game would also have been the first in  its medium to focus solely on the  legendary bounty hunter as opposed to  the many games in which he takes a more  sidelined role but unlike the movie  which many thought would be more of a  western story 1313 was to be an urban  crime story something resembling film  noir and mafia stories more than any  western at this point however it seems  that nobody will ever see this game in  any form which is certainly a real loss  to the franchise  an animated comedy developed by the  creators of robot chicken star wars  detours actually has 39 completed  episodes apparently though it didn't  quite fit with what disney had in mind  for the franchise when they bought it  that might seem surprising given the  huge success of the star wars robot  chicken sketches among fans clearly  george lucas was willing to let people  make jokes about his beloved franchise  and the fans would have loved it too  considering the trailer makes it clear  that the show is stuffed with all kinds  of references easter eggs and clever  jokes  r2  nobody's talking to you trash can  it also seems as though detours would  have been a great way to give more  screen time to characters who only  appear briefly in the movies such as  dexter jetstar who based on the trailer  seems to have been a main character on  the show while co-creator seth green has  said that there isn't any interest in  releasing the show anymore fans can  still hope that detours will eventually  see the light of day  do it for dexter disney star wars return  of the jedi ewok adventure was one of  two video games developed for release  alongside return of the jedi for some  reason though only its sibling death  star battle ever made its way to ataris  of course ewok adventure wouldn't be  developed for the atari today but the  idea of playing an entire game as an  ewok is undeniably appealing whether the  concept is retooled for something  grander or stays as little more than a  mobile game for example it's pretty easy  to imagine this concept being retored  into something like little big planet  giving players a tool to create maps  that include a variety of traps and  contraptions like those that ewoks  create in return of the jedi this could  also bring a community aspect to the  game that would allow players to share  their creations and fight together  against the invading empire  alternatively it's very easy to imagine  that the original game would be given a  fresher look or remaining little more  than a time sync mobile game either way  everyone loves ewoks and the video game  centering endor's vicious little teddy  bears would surely put smiles on a lot  of faces  battle of the sith lords was a star wars  video game that would have allowed  players to take on the role of a young  darth maul as he grows into a more  powerful sith lord albeit not entirely  of his own volition in fact the game  would have delved into how traumatizing  the training of a young sith lord can be  with maul being kidnapped by palpatine  as a child and tortured into taking on  the role of his apprentice sadly the  development of the game ran into  timeline and law issues with the  franchise's plans to bring more back as  a significant character in the clone  wars animated tv show once that happens  the game development team was left with  too little information to work from  while also being logged into new  canonical facts about maul's life  eventually after significant development  and a number of shifts in the game's  trajectory the game was cancelled this  isn't only a shame because the game  would have further developed the story  of a beloved character though that is  also true but it's also a last because  battle of the seth lords could have been  one of the franchise's most significant  moves into the realm of horror with a  key aspect of the game being the way  that maul used his own fear to  manipulate the fears of others sounds  pretty cool don't you think  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more luba videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

